# OPUS GUBERNATIO PARTICIPANT PACKAGE og-participant-2026.08-v26
#
# SUCCESSOR to og-participant-2026.08-v25, whose checksum record is preserved unchanged at
# code_audit/run62_participant_package_v25_checksums.sha256 and describes the tree as v25 left
# it. That record is NOT regenerated and NOT edited: it is pinned in
# server/tools/participant_packages.py to the explicit commit
# 5fec302c29c9f90256d74c1eeded1747d34e2900, the tip of `main` at which v25 was still current.
# The pin was established by BYTE COMPARISON of the record itself against that commit's blob and
# member by member over all sixty-nine members. Its header still says it describes the LIVE
# TREE, and that sentence is left exactly as it was, because rewriting a predecessor record to
# agree with the present is the failure B11 exists to catch. THIS record describes the LIVE TREE.
#
# RUN 63, THE FOUR CHARTS. TWO of the sixty-nine files moved: assets/js/detail.js and
# assets/js/neural_flow.js. None was added and none was deleted.
#
# NO SEQUENCE EXCEPTION IS CARRIED ACROSS THIS LINK, and that is DECLARED rather than omitted.
# The sequence-bearing set from v21 onward is five files -- assets/js/decision.js,
# assets/js/decision-ui.js, assets/js/workspace.js, assets/questionnaires/intake.json,
# assets/questionnaires/debrief.json. NEITHER of the two files that moved is a member of it,
# MEASURED against SEQUENCE_BEARING_FILES_FROM_V21 and not assumed, so
# V25_TO_V26_SEQUENCE_EXCEPTION is the EMPTY TUPLE and says so out loud. All five
# sequence-bearing files are present and byte for byte identical across this successor,
# MEASURED and not assumed. A sequence-bearing file moving WITHOUT being named there still
# turns the gate red.
#
# WHAT MOVED, AND WHY. The owner named four charts as broken. The Signal Flow reported
# "0 uploaded documents across 0 types" on a page listing 100 documents, and "2 estimable
# categories" where the Project Signal Network, on the same page and the same stored row, read
# "1 Amber, 10 No-data". Both were measured in a real browser before and after the change
# (server/tools/drive_run63_four_charts.py) against a fixture built to PRJ-001's shape.
#
#   assets/js/neural_flow.js -- the document count no longer comes from the window "since the
#   last signals_reset", a window that is permanently zero for a project that was reset and then
#   recomputed, because `projectcompute` re-reads the retained documents WITHOUT appending one
#   new `signals_extracted` event. It now calls LinDetail.uploadedDocEvents -- the Documents
#   panel's own reader -- gated on a LIVE stored row for the period the page holds, which is a
#   stronger form of Run 18's requirement rather than a weaker one. The browser-side worst-of
#   category fusion is removed: a category the stored row gives no status now reads as no data.
#
#   assets/js/detail.js -- exports that one document reader so the two surfaces cannot count
#   different sets, and grafts the served `source_documents` record onto the stored result so
#   LinResults.rowFor can answer with it.
#
# NO STEP OF THE DECISION SEQUENCE, no reveal gate, no lock, no randomization, no questionnaire
# and no append-only record moved. NO CONTROL was added, moved or removed. NO SERVER COMPUTATION
# MOVED: 101 registered, 63 in service, voting exactly A1.7 and A1.8, no stored figure changed,
# and the behaviour digest is RE-DERIVED and unchanged.
#
